==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|líða}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*līþaną}}. The senses “suffer, tolerate” may be borrowed from {{etyl|gml|is}}, but derive from the same root in any case.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈliːða/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|iːða|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|leið|liðu|liðið}}

# {{lb|is|transitive|governs the dative|of time}} to [[pass]], to [[go by]]{{jump|is|pass|d}}
#: {{usex|Ætluðum við ekki að hittast í vikunni sem '''leið'''?|Weren't we going to meet '''last''' week?|lang=is}}
#: {{usex|Tíminn '''líður'''.|Time '''goes by'''.|lang=is}}
#: {{usex|Þegar '''leið''' á daginn heyrðu þeir í drauginum sem bjó í fjallinu.|They heard the ghost in the mountain as the day grew old.|lang=is}}
# {{lb|is|intransitive}} to [[float]], to [[glide]]{{jump|is|glide|s}}
# {{lb|is|impersonal|intransitive}} describing a specific [[feeling]]; to [[feel]] {{jump|is|feel|s}}
#: {{usex|Hvernig '''líður''' þér? - ''Mér '''líður''' ekki vel.|How are you '''feeling'''? - I don't '''feel''' good.|lang=is}}
#: {{usex|Mér '''líður''' vel.|I '''feel''' good.|lang=is}}
#: {{usex|Okkur '''líður''' illa.|We '''feel''' bad.|lang=is}}
# {{lb|is|ambitransitive|governs the dative}} to [[progress]]{{jump|is|progress|s}}
#: {{usex|Hvernig '''líður''' náminu?|How are your '''studies''' progressing?|lang=is}}
# {{lb|is|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[suffer]]{{jump|is|suffer|s}}
#: {{usex|Þú munt '''líða''' fyrir það sem vinir þínir gerðu.|You shall '''suffer''' for what your friends did.|lang=is}}
# {{lb|is|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[endure]], to [[tolerate]]{{jump|is|tolerate|s}}
#: {{usex|Ég '''líð''' ekki svona vitleysu!|I do not '''tolerate''' this kind of nonsense!|lang=is}}

